  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Tetracycline is an antibiotic used against bacterial infections such as acne, gonorrhea, chlamydia, rickettsial infections and bronchitis. It remains an approved medicine, including veterinary use, and is listed among WHO essential medicines, though some products have been withdrawn in places.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q193045&quot;>Wikidata Q193045</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>tetracycline</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>A01AB13, D06AA04, J01AA07, S01AA09, S02AA08, S03AA02</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB00759&quot;>DB00759</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/54675776&quot;>54675776</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:27902&quot;>27902</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q193045&quot;>Q193045</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C22H24N2O8</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>444.44 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
